Your .env mapping matches the CamPay dashboard:

App Username → CAMPAY_USERNAME
App Password → CAMPAY_PASSWORD
App webhook key → CAMPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET
App ID → CAMPAY_APP_ID (widget only — do not use the Widget integration JS in FlowPay)
Ignore the Widget integration page
That snippet (campay.js, payButtonId, onSuccess) is for embedding CamPay on a merchant site. FlowPay already collects via the server adapter (/api/collect/ on confirm). You do not need to paste or save that widget code.

One thing you still need: public webhooks
CamPay cannot reach http://127.0.0.1:3011. Until a tunnel is set, payments may stay PROCESSING after MoMo approval.

Install ngrok (you had a signup tab open).
Run:
ngrok http 3011
Copy the https://….ngrok-free.app URL into .env:
FLOWPAY_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL=https://YOUR-SUBDOMAIN.ngrok-free.app
In CamPay → FlowPay app → Settings, set webhook/notify URL to:
https://YOUR-SUBDOMAIN.ngrok-free.app/api/v1/webhooks/CAMPAY
Restart the API (npm run dev in Flowpay/services/api).
Optional: paste Permanent Access token into CAMPAY_ACCESS_TOKEN to skip the token round-trip (username/password already work).

Test your first real payment
Open http://localhost:3025
Choose MTN Mobile Money
Use a customer phone CamPay demo accepts (e.g. 237670000001)
Complete MoMo on the phone
Confirm success only when status is SUCCEEDED (webhook received)
Re-check anytime:

cd Flowpay/services/api
npm run verify:campay
curl http://127.0.0.1:3011/api/v1/health
Look for "CAMPAY":"provider-sandbox".

Security: .env holds live secrets — do not commit it to git. If it was ever pushed, rotate keys in the CamPay portal.

After ngrok is running, paste your ngrok HTTPS URL (not the secrets) and we can confirm the webhook URL and run a full payment test together.

